WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Peru is a country in western South America, famous for its ancient Incan Empire.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Here, the historic road system 'Qhapaq Ñan' stretches across the Andean landscape.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Machu Picchu towers at 2,430 meters altitude in the eastern Cordillera of southern Peru.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Lake Titicaca on the southern border is the highest navigable lake in the world at 3,812 meters.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Traditional textiles are handwoven from native Alpaca and Vicuña wool across Cusco highlands.

